[statement]
As `a-candidate-whose-dependency-cannot-be-met-is-passed-over-beside-one-depending-further-up-through-a-provided-name`,
with `p2` the only provider of `w`: apk chooses `n` 2, which needs
`missing`, and refuses. From the only candidate for a name, not yet
installed, the chain of requirements goes on through the name the
candidate carries, `p2`, which nothing requires, so `p1` is not up the
chain.

